st value (6), remaining rows shift\n\nLet me implement this properly:\n\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    R, C = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Extract non-zero row values while preserving indices\n    row_data = []  # (original_row_index, row_value)\n    for r in range(R):\n        if not all(x == 0 for x in grid[r]):\n            # Check if row is constant (all same value)\n            if len(set(grid[r])) == 1:\n                val = grid[r][0]\n                row_data.append((r, val))\n            else:\n                return grid\n    \n    if len(row_data) == 0:\n        # All rows might be empty - return input or fill with pattern\n        return grid\n    \n    # Build output: output row i gets value from row_data[(i+1) % len(row_data)][1]\n    # But we need to fill all rows C cells each\n    output_grid = []\n    for r in range(R):\n        # Find matching row in original data\n        # The non-zero rows shift: output row 0 gets last non-zero row's value\n        # output row i gets value from row_data[(r) % len(row_data)][1] but adjusted\n        # Looking at demo: input[6]=4 goes to output[0]\n        # This is: output[r] = input[(r+1) % R].row_value if valid, else input[r].row_value\n        \n        if r < len(row_data):\n            # Original row r has a value\n            orig_val = row_data[r][1]\n            val = orig_val\n        else:\n            # Fill with last known value from the pattern\n            if row_data:\n                val = row_data[-1][1]\n            else:\n                val = 0\n        \n        output_grid.append([val] * C)\n    \n    return output_grid\n```\n\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":139,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793273494.924,"t1":1793273543.514,"alias":"task-7035319c","message":"Your program was checked on earlier pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 9 0 0 0